From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: File Explorer and Linux programs' frames follow a new display scale

explorer.exe is per-monitor aware (its manifest), and File Explorer sizes
itself by the system DPI it started with: with the display scale changed
while it was open (0890), it stayed the old scale's size -- tiny after
100% -> 175% -- and so was one opened afterwards in the same session's
old process. File Explorer is now aware of the system DPI only, and Wine
scales it to the new scale, as Windows does such a program. The frames of
Linux programs' windows are per-monitor v2: Wine draws their title bars at
the new scale while the program inside scales itself (sg-session's
XSETTINGS manager).

Test: test/dpilive-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_FE_PM in fileexplorer.c);
test/linuxembed-gate.sh, csdframe, ownframe, embeddragmax, embedmaxgrab,
linuxstandin still pass.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/fileexplorer.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/fileexplorer.c
@@ -5466,6 +5466,14 @@
     WCHAR path[MAX_PATH];
 
     if (open_fonts_folder(root)) return;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_FE_PM
+    /* Stained Glass OS: File Explorer is laid out at the system DPI (its
+     * S() sizes): when the display scale changes while it is open, Wine
+     * scales its window to the new one, as Windows does a program that is
+     * aware of the system DPI. As explorer.exe (its manifest: per-monitor)
+     * it stayed the old scale's size -- tiny after 100% -> 175%. */
+    SetThreadDpiAwarenessContext(DPI_AWARENESS_CONTEXT_SYSTEM_AWARE);
+#endif
     CoCreateInstance(&CLSID_ShellWindows, NULL, CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER, &IID_IShellWindows, (void **)&fe.sw);
 
     if (root && root[0] == ':' && root[1] == ':')
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -2104,7 +2104,14 @@
 #ifdef SG_MUTANT_NO_EMBED
     return NULL;
 #endif
-    frame = CreateWindowExW( WS_EX_APPWINDOW, L"SgLinuxWindow", title, WS_OVERLAPPEDWINDOW, 0, 0, 100, 100, 0, 0, 0, 0 );
+    {
+        /* Stained Glass OS: per-monitor v2, as the Linux program inside
+         * scales itself: Wine draws the frame at the display scale, a new
+         * one too (0890) */
+        DPI_AWARENESS_CONTEXT ctx = SetThreadDpiAwarenessContext( DPI_AWARENESS_CONTEXT_PER_MONITOR_AWARE_V2 );
+        frame = CreateWindowExW( WS_EX_APPWINDOW, L"SgLinuxWindow", title, WS_OVERLAPPEDWINDOW, 0, 0, 100, 100, 0, 0, 0, 0 );
+        SetThreadDpiAwarenessContext( ctx );
+    }
     if (!frame) return NULL;
     if (!(g = (ULONGLONG)sg_embed_call( frame, SG_EMBED_QUERY, xid ))) { DestroyWindow( frame ); return NULL; }
     rc.left = (short)(g & 0xffff);
